select 'sociological-theory', 'Structural functionalism: Theory', 'Functionalism also has an anthropological basis in the work of theorists such as Marcel Mauss, Bronisław Malinowski and Radcliffe-Brown. The prefix ''structural'' emerged in Radcliffe-Brown''s specific usage. Radcliffe-Brown proposed that most stateless, "primitive" societies, lacking strong centralized institutions, are based on an association of corporate-descent groups, i.e. the respective society''s recognised kinship groups. Structural functionalism also took on Malinowski''s argument that the basic building block of society is the nuclear family, and that the clan is an outgrowth, not vice versa. It is simplistic to equate the perspective directly with political conservatism. The tendency to emphasize "cohesive systems", however, leads functionalist theories to be contrasted with "conflict theories" which instead emphasize social problems and inequalities.', 'Wikipedia: Structural functionalism', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Structural_functionalism&oldid=1379034534', 'CC BY-SA 4.0. Wikipedia contributors (see page history). Excerpted and split into passages.'
where not exists (select 1 from public.content_chunks where topic_id = 'sociological-theory' and body = 'Functionalism also has an anthropological basis in the work of theorists such as Marcel Mauss, Bronisław Malinowski and Radcliffe-Brown. The prefix ''structural'' emerged in Radcliffe-Brown''s specific usage. Radcliffe-Brown proposed that most stateless, "primitive" societies, lacking strong centralized institutions, are based on an association of corporate-descent groups, i.e. the respective society''s recognised kinship groups. Structural functionalism also took on Malinowski''s argument that the basic building block of society is the nuclear family, and that the clan is an outgrowth, not vice versa. It is simplistic to equate the perspective directly with political conservatism. The tendency to emphasize "cohesive systems", however, leads functionalist theories to be contrasted with "conflict theories" which instead emphasize social problems and inequalities.');
