select 'sociological-theory', 'Symbolic interactionism', 'Symbolic interactionism is a sociological theory that develops from practical considerations and alludes to humans'' particular use of shared language to create common symbols and meanings, for use in both intra- and interpersonal communication. It is particularly important in microsociology and social psychology. It is derived from the American philosophy of pragmatism and particularly from the work of George Herbert Mead, as a pragmatic method to interpret social interactions.', 'Wikipedia: Symbolic interactionism', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Symbolic_interactionism&oldid=1381165710', 'CC BY-SA 4.0. Wikipedia contributors (see page history). Excerpted and split into passages.'
where not exists (select 1 from public.content_chunks where topic_id = 'sociological-theory' and body = 'Symbolic interactionism is a sociological theory that develops from practical considerations and alludes to humans'' particular use of shared language to create common symbols and meanings, for use in both intra- and interpersonal communication. It is particularly important in microsociology and social psychology. It is derived from the American philosophy of pragmatism and particularly from the work of George Herbert Mead, as a pragmatic method to interpret social interactions.');
